{"id":"sysc-greet-dev-1","content_hash":"4de9e2e7939b777ec6c466811e699180a6f5085873c95f4c77f89896851192f3","title":"Investigate authentication bug after incorrect password","description":"The authentication flow doesn't cancel sessions when authentication fails, leaving the IPC connection in a bad state. Root causes identified:\n\n1. **Missing session cleanup**: When authentication fails (wrong password), the created session is not cancelled, leaving the IPC connection in an undefined state.\n\n2. **Password memory issue**: The  receives a pointer to local password variable that becomes invalid after function returns.\n\n3. **Inconsistent error handling**: Some error paths don't properly reset the session state.\n\nThe user gets stuck because the IPC connection remains in a session that's awaiting authentication, preventing new login attempts from working properly until the entire greeter is restarted.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"bug","created_at":"2025-10-30T10:06:24.941380098+11:00","updated_at":"2025-10-30T10:10:00.765263558+11:00","closed_at":"2025-10-30T10:10:00.765263558+11:00"}
